## Part 3: Alphabet / Letter Based (41–60)

41. **AB, BC, CD, DE** — सब consecutive letter pairs; **All similar → No odd**.
42. **PQ, RS, TU, VW** — सब consecutive pairs; **No odd**.
43. **MN, OP, QR, ST** — सब consecutive; **No odd**.
44. **AX, BY, CZ, DW** — pattern: first letters A,B,C,D and second letters X,Y,Z,W — all follow mapping; **No odd**.
45. **QT** — KL,MN,OP are consecutive pairs; QT is not consecutive pair → **QT** odd.
46. **AB, EF, IJ, MN** — all are pairs separated by same gap? AB (1), EF (5,6), IJ (9,10), MN (13,14) — all are consecutive pairs — **No odd**.
47. **AZ, BY, CX, DU** — all are reverse-symmetric pairs (A-Z, B-Y...), pattern consistent — **No odd**.
48. **AB, AC, AD, AE** — AB is consecutive, others skip one; but pattern: all start with A then next letter varies — **No odd** (all start with A). If must choose, **AB** is only consecutive pair — but typical odd one out might be **AB** because others non-consecutive. I'll pick **AB**.
49. **LM, NO, PQ, ST** — all consecutive pairs — **No odd**.
50. **KL** — GH, HI, IJ are overlapping consecutive sequences? GH(7,8) HI(8,9) IJ(9,10) KL(11,12) all similar — **No odd**.
51. **AA, BB, CC, DD** — all double letters — **No odd**.
52. **PR** — PQ, QR, RS are consecutive overlapping pairs; PR is skip-one pair → **PR** odd.
53. **AB, CD, FG, IJ** — AB(1-2), CD(3-4), FG(6-7), IJ(9-10) — all are consecutive pairs — **No odd**.
54. **OP, QR, ST, VW** — all consecutive pairs — **No odd**.
55. **FU** — AZ, CY, EX, FU follow pattern of letters separated by 25, ... actually pattern: A-Z (1,26), C-Y(3,25), E-X(5,24), F-U(6,21) — all are symmetric pairs; **No odd**.
56. **BA, DC, FE, HG** — all reversed consecutive pairs — **No odd**.
57. **MN, NP, OP, PQ** — MN is consecutive, NP skips (N-P skip O) — NP is odd → **NP**.
58. **KM** — JK, KL, LM are consecutive overlapping; KM is non-consecutive → **KM**.
59. **RT** — PQ, LM, WX are non-consecutive mixed; hard — PQ (16-17), LM(12-13), WX(23-24) are consecutive; RT (18-20) skip one (R-T skip S) → **RT**.
60. **AA, AB, AC, AD** — AA is double same letter whereas others are different second letters — **AA** odd.

